# One rule instead of a list of extensions.
#
# The previous version pinned .md, .json, .yaml, .yml and .sh to LF and left
# .js to `text=auto`, which checks out CRLF on Windows. Prettier assumes LF, so
# every JavaScript file failed `format:check` on the Windows runner and nowhere
# else — a defect invisible to a working tree that was already normalized.
#
# Enumerating extensions means the next new one is wrong by default.
* text=auto eol=lf

# PowerShell is the one deliberate exception: some hosts still require CRLF.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
